From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:49:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upkeep U0: measured baseline + plan (UPKEEP_PLAN U0)

Open ROADMAP candidate #4 with a current-code and consumer
audit of the seven site-documented gaps. The baseline finds
that the shorthand "one upkeep patch" would combine unrelated
CPU reset, device, TCP, debugger and web-security semantics,
so it maps D1-D7 to U1-U7 with per-phase vectors, negative
controls and canaries.

Measured highlights: IA32_APIC_BASE is stored while LAPIC
decode/delivery remains fixed and SMP slots seed BSP=1; CF9
has full reset but no CPU-INIT request kind; the RTC has no
representation for a guest-set date; the north-star e1000
probe takes three EERD timeouts before RAL/RAH fallback;
responder TCP acks/appends without sequence validation, so
SACK cannot be honest yet; gdbstub zeroes now-real x87 state;
and loopback is the GUI/monitor's only access control.

Docs only. Targeted receipts: test-unit, test-tap-responder,
test-gui, test-monitor and the 30-check pure-RSP gdb lane are
green; real GNU gdb is absent on this host and is recorded
as a U3 gate requirement rather than a receipt.
